      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:144:1",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ السَّعْيِ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَ الْمَرْوَةِ عَلَى الدَّابَّةِ قَالَ نَعَمْ وَ عَلَى الْمَحْمِلِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about the Sa’ee performed  between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa upon the animal. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes, and upon the carriage’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who performs Sa‘y between al-Safa’ and al-Marwah riding on a stumper. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, he can do so as well as on a carriage.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
